WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.460
- [Mark] All right.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.890
Alfred.

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.490
Alfred, you're the pastor at
new St. John Baptist Church

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.110
of Houma-
- Yes.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.230
- [Mark] In Houma, Louisiana.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.170
- [Alfred] Yes.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.140
- [Mark] This is the heart
of Cajun country, right?

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.655
- Right.

00:00:16.655 --> 00:00:18.676
- [Mark] You grew up where?

00:00:18.676 --> 00:00:23.220
- I growed up, in fact,
right across the bayou

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:28.163
from the church and the
plantation was called,

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.943
and it's still called Presquille.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.570
- [Mark] So you've been
here your whole life.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.782
How old are you?

00:00:35.782 --> 00:00:37.057
- I'm 61.

00:00:37.057 --> 00:00:37.890
= [Mark] 61.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.070
And you grew up with both your parents?

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:43.050
- Yes, I did.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.230
- [Mark] Good childhood?

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.063
- Yes.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.470
- [Mark] And you became a man of faith

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:53.580
and a religious leader at
what point in your life?

00:00:54.482 --> 00:00:56.197
- Oh,

00:00:56.197 --> 00:00:58.320
it was 2006.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.480
- [Mark] You were raised
with a Baptist background?

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.899
- Yes.

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:04.930
- [Mark] And then in
2006, you became a pastor.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.973
- I became a pastor in 2006.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.440
- [Mark] So where do
you see what's going on

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.370
in our country with all the race issues

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.880
that are in the news right
now, black lives matter,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.894
what happened up in
Minnesota a while back?

00:01:20.894 --> 00:01:22.720
What do you, what do you make of it?

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.950
And what does your
congregation think of all this?

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:26.783
- Well,

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:30.243
to me,

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.880
it seems like

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.963
what's been going on,

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.633
no change is being made,

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.683
it's still happening.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:48.913
And

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.500
what is the reason

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.543
why this still going on?

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.497
And this been going on regular

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.893
for a short period of time,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.650
you know, it's not a space
it's like every two weeks

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.323
or something like that,
something like that happening.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.043
So,

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:23.740
I'm wondering

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.963
why this allowed to be.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:34.283
Well, this can't be
slowed down or stopped,

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.113
you know, they're protesting but,

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.683
look like the protesting not
doing too much of a good.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:47.113
The protesting behind these
things that's happening.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.760
So where do we go from here with this year

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.373
when it's steady happening?

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.883
I don't, I don't like,

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.503
taking no sides, but I like righteousness.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.900
Not taking no sides because of, you know

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.370
whatever your nationality may be.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:24.683
But I like justice in the right way.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.040
To me, I think

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.200
there's not enough discipline

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.613
with the police force.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.887
They not using enough
discipline with the policemens

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.820
in the actions that they
take when they doing stuff

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.653
like that.

00:04:06.587 --> 00:04:09.733
And I think as one get by

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.140
the other one believe that they can get by

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.423
doing it wrong too.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:23.090
And long as they continue
not using the discipline

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:28.610
that they need to use, I believe
that it's not gonna stop.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.160
- [Mark] You grew up in the South.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.853
Do you see how racism has,

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.610
has it diminished, has it
increased, has it changed

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:37.860
since you were a kid?

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:38.693
- Oh.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.313
Back in my childhood days,

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.023
at that time, it wasn't as bad.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.440
And I'm not talking about
the slavery time, I'm talking

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.310
about in my childhood time.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.660
- [Mark] There was segregation.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.290
- Yeah.

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:05.743
It wasn't that bad, well,
you had police brutality,

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.023
you know,

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.183
like it is now.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.823
Well, right now,

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:23.910
a lot has changed from my
time, from my childhood,

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.900
when it come down to the law itself,

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:30.703
not just police brutality, the law itself.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:36.240
A lot of changes have taken place

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:41.220
to where, just it not just being revealed

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.073
in a way that it should.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:44.840
- [Mark] So do you think racism

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:48.292
has increased or decreased or changed

00:05:48.292 --> 00:05:50.307
and maybe it's still around
and it looks different?

00:05:50.307 --> 00:05:52.250
- Ah, it have increased.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.410
- [Mark] You think increased?

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:57.057
- It have-
- Things are pretty bad now?

00:05:57.057 --> 00:05:58.409
- To me-
- Like in the 60s.

00:05:58.409 --> 00:05:59.242
- To me,

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.100
in one way

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:06.950
it have increased

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.180
in another way it haven't.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.940
- [Mark] Yeah, 'cause in
the 60s it was extreme

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:12.730
how blacks were kept totally separate.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:15.490
- Right, so now I'm
saying in one way it have

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:16.643
and another way,

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.173
it haven't.

00:06:20.173 --> 00:06:21.006
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:21.006 --> 00:06:24.310
What do you see the
church's role in all this?

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:29.310
I mean, what do you, do
you think religion can help

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.620
lead either the white

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:34.430
part of our population

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.990
or the black or all of the population

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.980
into something healthier
and something better

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:42.093
where we're treating each
other better and more fairly?

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:51.080
- Well, I know the, the
black denomination Baptist,

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:03.083
is like,

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:06.830
you can tell them

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.352
what to do and how to go about doing this

00:07:12.352 --> 00:07:13.502
where it will be better

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:21.370
and some just don't take no
heed to it and they fall back

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.820
on the church, like the
church not doing nothing.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.553
But the church is not doing
what it should be doing,

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.903
I can tell you that much,
we not doing what we,

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.680
what we really should be
doing, all of the things

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:42.690
we should be doing, but we
doing I think we're doing enough

00:07:44.074 --> 00:07:48.090
and some that still come,
be increased still though.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:50.160
I mean, be decreased to the increase

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.513
of what's going on right now, you know?

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:58.093
But the people got to do their part too.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.570
To make it work, we got to work together

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:05.887
to make this thing come
together like it should be,

00:08:05.887 --> 00:08:07.233
we got to work together.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.910
You just can't expect

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.780
one side to do this,

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:18.840
and then the other side, not
even trying to get on one

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:20.480
or call with the other side

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:26.953
I believe if we come together,
it'll be so much better.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:32.463
And like I say, I'm not a racist,

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:37.883
I don't care what color you
are, all of my body justice.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:40.333
That's it.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:43.760
- [Mark] I just came from Mississippi

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.280
and also here, in parts of Louisiana

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:49.253
there's some very poor communities.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.820
Some of the poorest in the country

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:58.050
and those are primarily
African-American communities.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.660
- Well, that's why I had

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.750
said what I said

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:07.750
about the black Baptist denomination,

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:10.303
the Baptist religious.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:13.140
It's not that

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.090
the pastors the preachers is not

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.293
putting it out there for them,

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.543
it's just that they not accepting it.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:31.550
If I tell you how to go about doing this

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:34.220
what to do and how to go
about doing, like I said

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.360
I was telling somebody the other day,

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.940
if you know that

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.080
this brutality is increasing

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.320
don't put yourself in the way of it.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.743
Try not to put yourself in the way of it.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:04.973
See, all we look at what
the policemen are did.

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:10.383
But we not looking at
what caused it to be.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:19.903
For example, if I don't want
no dealing with the policeman,

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:27.033
with the law, I'm gonna
try to not break the law.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.623
So they don't have, I don't
have to deal with them.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.570
You see what I'm saying?

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:38.490
But you got some of them breaking the law

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:43.490
and knowing what the consequences
might be behind it because

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.933
of what's going on and all this
police brutality, you know?

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.170
- [Mark] But what I've
seen is there's a lot

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.203
of black communities where,

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.280
for different reasons,
they were kept down.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.790
They're not, they're poorly
educated, very few opportunities

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.980
for them to make a substantial income

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.830
to support their families themselves.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:11.360
The whites kind of liked it that way,

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.543
or at least some of the whites
liked it that way in history.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.950
And eventually that comes back to snap you

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:21.920
in the butt because you can't
keep any race, any person down

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:27.120
for too long, eventually they're
going to react and revolt.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:30.130
And that's maybe what
we're seeing now is that

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:31.010
the black community feels

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:32.760
like they've been down for so long.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:35.273
No?

00:11:35.273 --> 00:11:36.370
- [Alfred] Oh yeah.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:37.203
Oh,

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.330
that's the way they feel

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:45.780
like they'd been down ever

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:49.500
since slavery, be honest with you.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.180
- Slavery, segregation-
- Segregation.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:52.770
- Poverty.
- Segregation

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.290
- [Mark] still going on today.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:57.653
- [Alfred] But when
segregation came about,

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.613
we had a little more freedom,

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:03.503
the blacks.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.870
We had a little more freedom

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:09.703
and

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:16.040
we could exercise our freedom,

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.630
if we wanted to.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.270
Some wanted to exercise their freedom

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:21.743
go further, some didn't.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:26.330
I don't want you to worry
about none of that, you know,

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:31.330
but then when it comes down to
where the situation they in,

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:34.743
they wanna point the finger the other way.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:41.240
So we have been down a
while, but we have been

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:46.240
having the opportunity to least get,

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:51.383
almost where we wanna be.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.790
Some just didn't take advantage of it.

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:57.623
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.290
In all your decades of
living in the South,

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:06.120
what's the most extreme
racism that you've seen?

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.733
Probably when you were
a kid, I would think.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:13.183
- Oh.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:21.393
In my childhood, I'm gonna
be honest with you there,

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:27.840
I didn't have no problem, and
I didn't see much of a problem

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.680
at that time, I guess,
maybe I wasn't looking at it

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.803
too in order to notice it,

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:40.540
but I never had problem of

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.440
another race doing me in,

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.440
treating me any kind of way.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:46.163
I ain't never had that problem.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:53.060
You know, when segregation came,
we went to the school along

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.620
with the others, you know,

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:58.820
and I ain't never had no problem,

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:02.140
not in school and not after school.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.040
I'm talking about me.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.900
I don't know about nobody else.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.480
- [Mark] As a kid, you were segregated?

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:07.500
- Huh?
- As a kid?

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.030
You were segregated in school.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:12.450
- Well, as a kid, I mean,
segregated mean that

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.940
we was given more freedom, more rights

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:19.550
to be able to go further in our lives

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:23.313
do things that we couldn't do once before.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.600
But coming up as a little child

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:34.290
I didn't never seen
nothing that was so drastic

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:39.580
and shown racism, you know, I
didn't see nothing like that.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:42.330
And I never had nothing like
that, that happened to me.

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:46.053
Never.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:50.190
- [Mark] Nothing like riding
in the back of the bus

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:51.023
separate like that?

00:14:51.023 --> 00:14:52.440
- Never had none of that experience.

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:53.540
- [Mark] None of that.

00:14:54.639 --> 00:14:55.650
Must've been earlier.

00:14:55.650 --> 00:15:00.650
- You know, I can say, I
can say that I was blessed

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:04.370
'cause, you know, I know there're others

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:07.223
that had many problems,

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:10.573
and I had had none.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:13.613
You know?

00:15:13.613 --> 00:15:17.393
I mean, so for, that's under cover,

00:15:18.898 --> 00:15:19.823
I might have been,

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:24.620
you know, might've been
racism under cover,

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:27.700
like, if I go apply for a job

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:28.533
and

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.380
they give the job to somebody else,

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:35.480
when they know that I was
more qualified for the job,

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:38.270
well, I can't say nothing
on it 'cause I don't know

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.663
if that happened to me.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:44.070
So for job wise, you
know, but everything else,

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.623
I ain't never had no problem.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:48.890
- [Mark] In your community,
in your congregation,

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:49.927
do you think people,

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:55.280
your congregation is
100% African-American?

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:56.113
- Yeah.

00:15:56.113 --> 00:15:57.250
- [Mark] And do they feel

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.970
kept down or just do they feel

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.650
like they're being cheated in any way?

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:20.343
- To tell you I never had

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:28.303
one of my members come to
me with a problem of racism.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.710
Like, for example, what then took place

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:37.573
with the police brutality,

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.920
I never had a member to come to me

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:48.880
and discussing that to me
and how they feel about it

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:50.080
and everything, never.

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:52.603
So my members,

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:55.490
when something's going down

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.923
and if it not right,

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:00.203
they usually,

00:17:00.203 --> 00:17:03.631
to me, don't make no fuss about it.

00:17:03.631 --> 00:17:05.830
They don't say, they don't, you know.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.240
- [Mark] Are you
optimistic for the future?

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:11.073
For our country?

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:20.383
- If I can have my say with that?

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:24.173
Oh, well.

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:29.193
I couldn't tell you
right now, but I think,

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:32.140
give it a few years, I'll know something.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:36.930
Give it a few years,
